# Frontend

- Stack: React + TypeScript + Vite, plus Tailwind and React Router. Tailwind and React Router are not installed yet; the first ticket that needs one adds it.
- Component-local state and focused hooks; no global state package.
- Each lyric unit stacks, in this order at every width: **Japanese**, **Pronunciation (Romaji)**, **Direct Meaning**. Use those exact labels.
- Japanese text gets `lang="ja"`. Render imported text as plain React text, never as HTML.
- Layer visibility lives in `sessionStorage`; at least one layer stays visible; invalid stored values fall back to all visible.
- The player has only the approved controls and only reports the playhead. Learn Song picks the current line from `startSeconds`. Follow scrolls to it, and scrolling by hand turns follow off. No tempo control.
- Accessibility: semantic landmarks, headings, and lists; labelled controls with pressed, muted, and value state; visible focus; reduced motion respected; never rely on color alone.
- Every async boundary has loading, success or empty, recoverable error with retry, and unknown error states.
- `src/contracts.ts` mirrors `backend/app/contracts.py`; change both together.
- Run frontend commands from `frontend/`.
